#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus percuma IBM tentang maklumat dan pengiraan kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simon's algorithm"
msgstr "Algoritma Simon"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore Leftrightarrow */}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore Leftrightarrow */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simon's algorithm is a quantum query algorithm for a problem known as *Simon's problem*.\n"
"This is a promise problem with a flavor similar to the Deutsch-Jozsa and Bernstein-Vazirani problems, but the specifics are different.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Simon ialah algoritma pertanyaan kuantum untuk masalah yang dikenali sebagai *masalah Simon*.\n"
"Ini adalah masalah janji yang mempunyai ciri serupa dengan masalah Deutsch-Jozsa dan Bernstein-Vazirani, tetapi butiran teknikalnya berbeza.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simon's algorithm is significant because it provides an *exponential* "
"advantage of quantum over classical (including probabilistic) algorithms, "
"and the technique it uses inspired Peter Shor's discovery of an efficient "
"quantum algorithm for integer factorization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Simon penting kerana ia memberikan kelebihan *eksponen* kuantum "
"berbanding algoritma klasik (termasuk kebarangkalian), dan teknik yang "
"digunakannya mengilhamkan Peter Shor untuk menemui algoritma kuantum cekap "
"bagi pemfaktoran integer.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Simon's problem {#simons-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah Simon {#simons-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The input function for Simon's problem takes the form\n"
msgstr "Fungsi input untuk masalah Simon berbentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma^m\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma^m\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for positive integers $n$ and $m.$\n"
"We could restrict our attention to the case $m = n$ in the interest of simplicity, but there's little to be gained in making this assumption — Simon's algorithm and its analysis are basically the same either way.\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk integer positif $n$ dan $m.$\n"
"Kita boleh mengehadkan perhatian kepada kes $m = n$ demi kesederhanaan, tetapi tiada manfaat besar dalam membuat andaian ini — algoritma Simon dan analisisnya pada dasarnya sama dalam kedua-dua keadaan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Simon's problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma^m$ \\\n"
"Promise: there exists a string $s\\in\\Sigma^n$ such that $[f(x) = f(y)] \\Leftrightarrow\n"
"[(x = y) \\vee (x \\oplus s = y)]$ for all $x,y\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: the string $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Masalah Simon\">\n"
"Input: fungsi $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma^m$ \\\n"
"Janji: wujud suatu rentetan $s\\in\\Sigma^n$ sedemikian sehingga $[f(x) = f(y)] \\Leftrightarrow\n"
"[(x = y) \\vee (x \\oplus s = y)]$ untuk semua $x,y\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: rentetan $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll unpack the promise to better understand what it says momentarily, but first let's be clear that it requires that $f$ has a very special structure — so most functions won't satisfy this promise.\n"
"It's also fitting to acknowledge that this problem isn't intended to have practical importance.\n"
"Rather, it's a somewhat artificial problem tailor-made to be easy for quantum computers and hard for classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menguraikan janji tersebut untuk memahami maknanya sebentar lagi, tetapi mula-mula kita perlu jelas bahawa janji ini mensyaratkan $f$ mempunyai struktur yang sangat istimewa — jadi kebanyakan fungsi tidak akan memenuhi janji ini.\n"
"Perlu juga diakui bahawa masalah ini tidak bertujuan untuk mempunyai kepentingan praktikal.\n"
"Sebaliknya, ia adalah masalah yang agak tiruan, dicipta khas untuk mudah diselesaikan oleh komputer kuantum tetapi sukar bagi komputer klasik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are two main cases: the first case is that $s$ is the all-zero string "
"$0^n,$ and the second case is that $s$ is not the all-zero string.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat dua kes utama: kes pertama ialah $s$ ialah rentetan semua-sifar "
"$0^n,$ dan kes kedua ialah $s$ bukan rentetan semua-sifar.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Case 1: $s=0^n.$\n"
"If $s$ is the all-zero string, then we can simplify the if and only if statement in the promise so that it reads $[f(x) = f(y)] \\Leftrightarrow [x = y].$\n"
"This is equivalent to $f$ being a one-to-one function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kes 1: $s=0^n.$\n"
"Jika $s$ ialah rentetan semua-sifar, kita boleh memudahkan pernyataan jika dan hanya jika dalam janji supaya ia berbunyi $[f(x) = f(y)] \\Leftrightarrow [x = y].$\n"
"Ini bersamaan dengan $f$ menjadi fungsi satu-ke-satu.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Case 2: $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
"If $s$ is not the all-zero string, then the promise being satisfied for this string implies that $f$ is *two-to-one*, meaning that for every possible output string of $f,$ there are exactly two input strings that cause $f$ to output that string. Moreover, these two input strings must take the form $w$ and $w \\oplus s$ for some string $w.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kes 2: $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
"Jika $s$ bukan rentetan semua-sifar, maka janji yang dipenuhi untuk rentetan ini bermakna $f$ adalah *dua-ke-satu*, iaitu untuk setiap rentetan output yang mungkin bagi $f,$ terdapat tepat dua rentetan input yang menyebabkan $f$ menghasilkan rentetan itu. Selain itu, kedua-dua rentetan input tersebut mesti berbentuk $w$ dan $w \\oplus s$ untuk suatu rentetan $w.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's important to recognize that there can only be one string $s$ that works"
" if the promise is met, so there's always a unique correct answer for "
"functions that satisfy the promise.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penting untuk diketahui bahawa hanya boleh ada satu rentetan $s$ yang "
"berfungsi jika janji dipenuhi, jadi sentiasa ada jawapan yang unik dan betul"
" untuk fungsi yang memenuhi janji.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's an example of a function taking the form $f:\\Sigma^3 \\rightarrow "
"\\Sigma^5$ that satisfies the promise for the string $s = 011.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah contoh fungsi berbentuk $f:\\Sigma^3 \\rightarrow \\Sigma^5$ "
"yang memenuhi janji untuk rentetan $s = 011.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(000) & = 10011 \\\\\n"
"f(001) & = 00101 \\\\\n"
"f(010) & = 00101 \\\\\n"
"f(011) & = 10011 \\\\\n"
"f(100) & = 11010 \\\\\n"
"f(101) & = 00001 \\\\\n"
"f(110) & = 00001 \\\\\n"
"f(111) & = 11010\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(000) & = 10011 \\\\\n"
"f(001) & = 00101 \\\\\n"
"f(010) & = 00101 \\\\\n"
"f(011) & = 10011 \\\\\n"
"f(100) & = 11010 \\\\\n"
"f(101) & = 00001 \\\\\n"
"f(110) & = 00001 \\\\\n"
"f(111) & = 11010\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are $8$ different input strings and $4$ different output strings, each of which occurs twice — so this is a two-to-one function.\n"
"Moreover, for any two different input strings that produce the same output string, we see that the bitwise XOR of these two input strings is equal to $011,$ which is equivalent to saying that either one of them equals the other XORed with $s.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat $8$ rentetan input yang berbeza dan $4$ rentetan output yang berbeza, setiap satunya muncul dua kali — jadi ini adalah fungsi dua-ke-satu.\n"
"Selain itu, bagi mana-mana dua rentetan input berbeza yang menghasilkan rentetan output yang sama, kita dapati bahawa XOR bitwise bagi kedua-dua rentetan input tersebut adalah sama dengan $011,$ yang bersamaan dengan mengatakan bahawa salah satunya adalah sama dengan yang satu lagi di-XOR dengan $s.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that the only thing that matters about the actual output strings is whether they're the same or different for different choices of input strings.\n"
"For instance, in the example above, there are four strings $(10011,$ $00101,$ $00001,$ and $11010)$ that appear as outputs of $f.$ We could replace these four strings with different strings, so long as they're all distinct, and the correct solution $s = 011$ would not change.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa satu-satunya perkara yang penting tentang rentetan output sebenar ialah sama ada ia sama atau berbeza bagi pilihan rentetan input yang berlainan.\n"
"Contohnya, dalam contoh di atas, terdapat empat rentetan $(10011,$ $00101,$ $00001,$ dan $11010)$ yang muncul sebagai output $f.$ Kita boleh menggantikan keempat-empat rentetan ini dengan rentetan lain, asalkan semuanya berbeza, dan penyelesaian yang betul $s = 011$ tidak akan berubah.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm description {#algorithm-description}"
msgstr "Penerangan algoritma {#algorithm-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here's a quantum circuit diagram representing Simon's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah gambar rajah Circuit kuantum yang mewakili algoritma Simon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Simon's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Simon.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Algoritma Simon](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Simon.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, there are $n$ qubits on the top that are acted upon by Hadamard gates and $m$ qubits on the bottom that go directly into the query gate.\n"
"It looks very similar to the algorithms we've already discussed in the lesson, but this time there's no phase kickback; the bottom $m$ qubits all go into the query gate in the state $\\vert 0\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk jelasnya, terdapat $n$ qubit di bahagian atas yang dikenakan gate Hadamard dan $m$ qubit di bahagian bawah yang masuk terus ke gate pertanyaan.\n"
"Ia kelihatan sangat serupa dengan algoritma yang telah kita bincangkan dalam pelajaran ini, tetapi kali ini tiada kickback fasa; $m$ qubit di bahagian bawah semuanya masuk ke dalam gate pertanyaan dalam keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To solve Simon's problem using this circuit will actually require several "
"independent runs of it followed by a classical post-processing step, which "
"will be described later after the behavior of the circuit is analyzed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menyelesaikan masalah Simon menggunakan Circuit ini sebenarnya "
"memerlukan beberapa kali jalankan bebas diikuti dengan langkah pemprosesan "
"pascaklasik, yang akan diterangkan kemudian selepas tingkah laku Circuit "
"dianalisis.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The analysis of Simon's algorithm begins along similar lines to the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"After the first layer of Hadamard gates is performed on the top $n$ qubits, the state becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Analisis algoritma Simon bermula dengan cara yang serupa dengan algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"
"Selepas lapisan gate Hadamard pertama dilakukan pada $n$ qubit teratas, keadaan menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert 0^m \\rangle \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert 0^m \\rangle \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the $U_f$ is performed, the output of the function $f$ is XORed onto "
"the all-zero state of the bottom $m$ qubits, so the state becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila $U_f$ dilakukan, output fungsi $f$ di-XOR ke keadaan semua-sifar "
"bagi $m$ qubit bahagian bawah, jadi keadaan menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the second layer of Hadamard gates is performed, we obtain the "
"following state by using the same formula for the action of a layer of "
"Hadamard gates as before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila lapisan gate Hadamard kedua dilakukan, kita memperoleh keadaan "
"berikut dengan menggunakan formula yang sama untuk tindakan lapisan gate "
"Hadamard seperti sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, the analysis diverges from the ones for the previous "
"algorithms in this lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada ketika ini, analisis menyimpang daripada analisis algoritma-algoritma "
"sebelumnya dalam pelajaran ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We're interested in the probability for the measurements to result in each possible string $y\\in\\Sigma^n.$\n"
"Through the rules for analyzing measurements described in the *Multiple systems* lesson of the *Basics of quantum information* course, we find that the probability $p(y)$ to obtain the string $y$ is equal to\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita berminat dengan kebarangkalian untuk pengukuran menghasilkan setiap rentetan yang mungkin $y\\in\\Sigma^n.$\n"
"Melalui peraturan untuk menganalisis pengukuran yang diterangkan dalam pelajaran *Sistem berganda* dalam kursus *Asas maklumat kuantum*, kita dapati bahawa kebarangkalian $p(y)$ untuk mendapatkan rentetan $y$ adalah sama dengan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) = \\left\\|\\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\right\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) = \\left\\|\\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\right\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To get a better handle on these probabilities, we'll need just a bit more notation and terminology.\n"
"First, the *range* of the function $f$ is the set containing all of its output strings.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memahami kebarangkalian ini dengan lebih baik, kita perlukan sedikit lagi notasi dan terminologi.\n"
"Pertama, *julat* fungsi $f$ ialah set yang mengandungi semua rentetan outputnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{range}(f) = \\{ f(x) : x\\in \\Sigma^n \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{range}(f) = \\{ f(x) : x\\in \\Sigma^n \\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second, for each string $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f),$ we can express the "
"set of all input strings that cause the function to evaluate to this output "
"string $z$ as $f^{-1}(\\{z\\}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua, untuk setiap rentetan $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f),$ kita boleh "
"menyatakan set semua rentetan input yang menyebabkan fungsi menilai kepada "
"rentetan output $z$ ini sebagai $f^{-1}(\\{z\\}).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f^{-1}(\\{z\\}) = \\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = z \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f^{-1}(\\{z\\}) = \\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = z \\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The set $f^{-1}(\\{z\\})$ is known as the *preimage* of $\\{z\\}$ under $f.$\n"
"We can define the preimage under $f$ of any set in place of $\\{z\\}$ in an analogous way — it's the set of all elements that $f$ maps to that set.\n"
"(This notation should not be confused with the *inverse* of the function $f,$ which may not exist.\n"
"The fact that the argument on the left-hand side is the set $\\{z\\}$ rather than the element $z$ is the clue that allows us to avoid this confusion.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Set $f^{-1}(\\{z\\})$ dikenali sebagai *praimej* bagi $\\{z\\}$ di bawah $f.$\n"
"Kita boleh mentakrifkan praimej di bawah $f$ bagi mana-mana set sebagai ganti $\\{z\\}$ dengan cara yang serupa — ia adalah set semua unsur yang dipetakan oleh $f$ ke set tersebut.\n"
"(Notasi ini tidak boleh dikelirukan dengan *songsangan* fungsi $f,$ yang mungkin tidak wujud.\n"
"Fakta bahawa argumen di sebelah kiri ialah set $\\{z\\}$ dan bukan unsur $z$ adalah petanda yang membolehkan kita mengelakkan kekeliruan ini.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using this notation, we can split up the sum in our expression for the probabilities above\n"
"to obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan notasi ini, kita boleh memisahkan jumlah dalam ungkapan kebarangkalian di atas\n"
"untuk mendapatkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) =\n"
"\\left\\|\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y}\\Biggr)\n"
"\\vert z \\rangle\n"
"\\right\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) =\n"
"\\left\\|\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y}\\Biggr)\n"
"\\vert z \\rangle\n"
"\\right\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ is represented exactly once by the two "
"summations — we're basically just putting these strings into separate "
"buckets depending on which output string $z = f(x)$ they produce when we "
"evaluate the function $f,$ and then summing separately over all the "
"buckets.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap rentetan $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ diwakili tepat sekali oleh dua penjumlahan "
"— pada dasarnya kita hanya memasukkan rentetan-rentetan ini ke dalam baldi "
"berasingan bergantung pada rentetan output $z = f(x)$ yang dihasilkan "
"apabila kita menilai fungsi $f,$ kemudian menjumlahkan secara berasingan ke "
"atas semua baldi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can now evaluate the Euclidean norm squared to obtain\n"
msgstr "Kita kini boleh menilai kuasa dua norma Euclidean untuk mendapatkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}}\n"
"\\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}}\n"
"\\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simplify these probabilities further, let's take a look at the value\n"
msgstr "Untuk memudahkan lagi kebarangkalian ini, mari kita lihat nilai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for an arbitrary selection of $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
msgstr "untuk pemilihan sewenang-wenangnya bagi $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If it happens to be the case that $s = 0^n,$ then $f$ is a one-to-one function and there's always just a single element $x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\}),$ for every $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
"The value of the expression $(1)$ is $1$ in this case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekiranya $s = 0^n,$ maka $f$ adalah fungsi satu-ke-satu dan sentiasa hanya ada satu unsur $x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\}),$ untuk setiap $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
"Nilai ungkapan $(1)$ adalah $1$ dalam kes ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If, on the other hand, $s\\neq 0^n,$ then there are exactly two strings in the set $f^{-1}(\\{z\\}).$\n"
"To be precise, if we choose $w\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})$ to be any one of these two strings, then the other string must be\n"
"$w \\oplus s$ by the promise in Simon's problem.\n"
"Using this observation we can simplify $(1)$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, jika $s\\neq 0^n,$ maka terdapat tepat dua rentetan dalam set $f^{-1}(\\{z\\}).$\n"
"Secara tepat, jika kita memilih $w\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})$ sebagai salah satu daripada dua rentetan ini, maka rentetan yang satu lagi mesti adalah\n"
"$w \\oplus s$ mengikut janji dalam masalah Simon.\n"
"Menggunakan pemerhatian ini kita boleh memudahkan $(1)$ seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert (-1)^{w\\cdot y} + (-1)^{(w\\oplus s)\\cdot y} \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert (-1)^{w\\cdot y} \\Bigl(1 + (-1)^{s\\cdot y}\\Bigr) \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert 1 + (-1)^{y\\cdot s} \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"4 & y \\cdot s = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & y \\cdot s = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert (-1)^{w\\cdot y} + (-1)^{(w\\oplus s)\\cdot y} \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert (-1)^{w\\cdot y} \\Bigl(1 + (-1)^{s\\cdot y}\\Bigr) \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert 1 + (-1)^{y\\cdot s} \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"4 & y \\cdot s = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & y \\cdot s = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, it turns out that the value $(1)$ is independent of the specific choice "
"of $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)$ in both cases.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, ternyata nilai $(1)$ adalah bebas daripada pilihan "
"$z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)$ yang spesifik dalam kedua-dua kes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now finish off the analysis by looking at the same two cases as "
"before separately.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini boleh menyelesaikan analisis dengan melihat dua kes yang sama "
"seperti sebelumnya secara berasingan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Case 1: $s = 0^n.$ In this case the function $f$ is one-to-one, so there are"
" $2^n$ strings $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f),$ and we obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Kes 1: $s = 0^n.$ Dalam kes ini fungsi $f$ adalah satu-ke-satu, jadi "
"terdapat $2^n$ rentetan $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f),$ dan kita mendapat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  p(y) = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}} \\cdot 2^n = \\frac{1}{2^n}.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  p(y) = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}} \\cdot 2^n = \\frac{1}{2^n}.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In words, the measurements result in a string $y\\in\\Sigma^n$ chosen "
"uniformly at random.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Dengan kata-kata, pengukuran menghasilkan rentetan $y\\in\\Sigma^n$ yang "
"dipilih secara seragam rawak.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Case 2: $s \\neq 0^n.$\n"
"In this case $f$ is two-to-one, so there are $2^{n-1}$ elements in $\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
"Using the formula from above we conclude that the probability to measure each $y\\in\\Sigma^n$ is\n"
msgstr ""
"Kes 2: $s \\neq 0^n.$\n"
"Dalam kes ini $f$ adalah dua-ke-satu, jadi terdapat $2^{n-1}$ unsur dalam $\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
"Menggunakan formula di atas kita simpulkan bahawa kebarangkalian untuk mengukur setiap $y\\in\\Sigma^n$ ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  p(y)\n"
"  = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}} \\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"  \\Biggl\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"  =\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2^{n-1}} & y \\cdot s = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & y \\cdot s = 1\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  p(y)\n"
"  = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}} \\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"  \\Biggl\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"  =\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2^{n-1}} & y \\cdot s = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & y \\cdot s = 1\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In words, we obtain a string chosen uniformly at random from the set $\\{y\\in\\Sigma^n : y \\cdot s = 0\\},$ which\n"
"  contains $2^{n-1}$ strings. (Because $s\\neq 0^n,$ exactly half of the binary strings of length $n$ have binary dot\n"
"  product $1$ with $s$ and the other have binary dot product $0$ with $s,$ as we already observed in the analysis of\n"
"  the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem.)\n"
msgstr ""
"  Dengan kata-kata, kita mendapat rentetan yang dipilih secara seragam rawak daripada set $\\{y\\in\\Sigma^n : y \\cdot s = 0\\},$ yang\n"
"  mengandungi $2^{n-1}$ rentetan. (Kerana $s\\neq 0^n,$ tepat separuh daripada rentetan binari panjang $n$ mempunyai hasil darab titik binari $1$ dengan $s$ dan separuh lagi mempunyai hasil darab titik binari $0$ dengan $s,$ seperti yang sudah kita perhatikan dalam analisis\n"
"  algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa untuk masalah Bernstein-Vazirani.)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical post-processing {#classical-post-processing}"
msgstr "Pemprosesan pascaklasik {#classical-post-processing}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now know what the probabilities are for the possible measurement outcomes when we run the quantum circuit for Simon's algorithm.\n"
"Is this enough information to determine $s$?\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini tahu apakah kebarangkalian bagi hasil pengukuran yang mungkin apabila kita menjalankan Circuit kuantum untuk algoritma Simon.\n"
"Adakah maklumat ini cukup untuk menentukan $s$?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is yes, provided that we're willing to repeat the process several times and accept that it could fail with some probability, which we can make very small by running the circuit enough times.\n"
"The essential idea is that each execution of the circuit provides us with statistical evidence concerning $s,$ and we can use that evidence to find $s$ with very high probability if we run the circuit sufficiently many times.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jawapannya ya, dengan syarat kita sanggup mengulangi proses beberapa kali dan menerima bahawa ia boleh gagal dengan suatu kebarangkalian, yang boleh kita jadikan sangat kecil dengan menjalankan Circuit cukup banyak kali.\n"
"Idea pokoknya ialah setiap pelaksanaan Circuit memberikan kita bukti statistik tentang $s,$ dan kita boleh menggunakan bukti itu untuk mencari $s$ dengan kebarangkalian yang sangat tinggi jika kita menjalankan Circuit cukup banyak kali.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's suppose that we run the circuit independently $k$ times, for $k = n + 10.$\n"
"There's nothing special about this particular number of iterations — we could take $k$ to be larger (or smaller) depending on the probability of failure we're willing to tolerate, as we will see.\n"
"Choosing $k = n + 10$ will ensure that we have greater than a $99.9$% chance of recovering $s.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Katakan kita menjalankan Circuit secara bebas $k$ kali, untuk $k = n + 10.$\n"
"Tiada yang istimewa tentang bilangan iterasi tertentu ini — kita boleh menjadikan $k$ lebih besar (atau lebih kecil) bergantung pada kebarangkalian kegagalan yang kita sanggup tolak, seperti yang akan kita lihat.\n"
"Memilih $k = n + 10$ akan memastikan kita mempunyai lebih daripada $99.9$% peluang untuk memulihkan $s.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By running the circuit $k$ times, we obtain strings $y^1,...,y^{k} \\in \\Sigma^n.$\n"
"To be clear, the superscripts here are part of the names of these strings, not exponents or indexes to their bits, so we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan menjalankan Circuit $k$ kali, kita mendapat rentetan $y^1,...,y^{k} \\in \\Sigma^n.$\n"
"Untuk jelasnya, superskrip di sini adalah sebahagian daripada nama rentetan-rentetan ini, bukan eksponen atau indeks kepada bit mereka, jadi kita ada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"y^1 & = y^1_{n-1} \\cdots y^1_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^2 & = y^2_{n-1} \\cdots y^2_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& \\;\\; \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^{k} & = y^{k}_{n-1} \\cdots y^{k}_{0}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"y^1 & = y^1_{n-1} \\cdots y^1_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^2 & = y^2_{n-1} \\cdots y^2_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& \\;\\; \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^{k} & = y^{k}_{n-1} \\cdots y^{k}_{0}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now form a matrix $M$ having $k$ rows and $n$ columns by taking the bits "
"of these strings as binary-valued entries.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini membentuk matriks $M$ yang mempunyai $k$ baris dan $n$ lajur "
"dengan mengambil bit rentetan-rentetan ini sebagai entri bernilai binari.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
" y^1_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^1_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
" y^2_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^2_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
" \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\[1mm]\n"
" y^{k}_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^{k}_{0}\n"
" \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
" y^1_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^1_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
" y^2_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^2_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
" \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\[1mm]\n"
" y^{k}_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^{k}_{0}\n"
" \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, we don't know what $s$ is at this point — our goal is to find this string.\n"
"But imagine for a moment that we do know the string $s,$ and we form a column vector $v$ from the bits of the string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, kita tidak tahu apa itu $s$ pada ketika ini — matlamat kita adalah untuk mencari rentetan ini.\n"
"Tetapi bayangkan sebentar bahawa kita memang tahu rentetan $s,$ dan kita membentuk vektor lajur $v$ daripada bit rentetan $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"v = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"s_{n-1}\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"s_0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"v = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"s_{n-1}\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"s_0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we perform the matrix-vector multiplication $M v$ modulo $2$ — meaning "
"that we perform the multiplication as usual and then take the remainder of "
"the entries of the result after dividing by $2$ — we obtain the all-zero "
"vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kita melakukan pendaraban matriks-vektor $M v$ modulo $2$ — bermakna "
"kita melakukan pendaraban seperti biasa dan kemudian mengambil baki entri "
"keputusan selepas dibahagi dengan $2$ — kita mendapat vektor semua-sifar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M v = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"y^1 \\cdot s\\\\\n"
"y^2 \\cdot s\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^{k} \\cdot s\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\\n"
"0\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M v = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"y^1 \\cdot s\\\\\n"
"y^2 \\cdot s\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^{k} \\cdot s\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\\n"
"0\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, treated as a column vector $v$ as just described, the string $s$ will always be an element of the *null space* of the matrix $M,$ provided that we do the arithmetic modulo $2.$\n"
"This is true in both the case that $s = 0^n$ and $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
"To be more precise, the all-zero vector is always in the null space of $M,$ and it's joined by the vector whose entries are the bits of $s$ in case $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Iaitu, diperlakukan sebagai vektor lajur $v$ seperti yang baru diterangkan, rentetan $s$ akan sentiasa menjadi unsur dalam *ruang nol* matriks $M,$ dengan syarat kita melakukan aritmetik modulo $2.$\n"
"Ini benar dalam kedua-dua kes $s = 0^n$ dan $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
"Lebih tepat lagi, vektor semua-sifar sentiasa berada dalam ruang nol $M,$ dan ia disertai oleh vektor yang entri-entrinya adalah bit $s$ sekiranya $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The question remaining is whether there will be any other vectors in the null space of $M$ besides the ones corresponding to $0^n$ and $s.$\n"
"The answer is that this becomes increasingly unlikely as $k$ increases — and if we choose $k = n + 10,$ the null space of $M$ will contain no other vectors in addition to those corresponding to $0^n$ and $s$ with greater than a $99.9$% chance.\n"
"More generally, if we replace $k = n + 10$ with $k = n + r$ for an arbitrary choice of a positive integer $r,$ the probability that the vectors corresponding to $0^n$ and $s$ are alone in the null space of $M$ is at least $1 - 2^{-r}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Persoalan yang masih ada ialah sama ada akan ada vektor lain dalam ruang nol $M$ selain daripada yang sepadan dengan $0^n$ dan $s.$\n"
"Jawapannya ialah ini menjadi semakin tidak mungkin apabila $k$ bertambah — dan jika kita memilih $k = n + 10,$ ruang nol $M$ tidak akan mengandungi vektor lain selain daripada yang sepadan dengan $0^n$ dan $s$ dengan lebih daripada $99.9$% peluang.\n"
"Secara lebih umum, jika kita menggantikan $k = n + 10$ dengan $k = n + r$ untuk pilihan integer positif $r$ yang sewenang-wenangnya, kebarangkalian bahawa vektor yang sepadan dengan $0^n$ dan $s$ bersendirian dalam ruang nol $M$ adalah sekurang-kurangnya $1 - 2^{-r}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using linear algebra, it is possible to efficiently calculate a description of the null space of $M$ modulo $2.$\n"
"Specifically, it can be done using *Gaussian elimination*, which works the same way when arithmetic is done modulo $2$ as it does with real or complex numbers.\n"
"So long as the vectors corresponding to $0^n$ and $s$ are alone in the null space of $M,$ which happens with high probability, we can deduce $s$ from the results of this computation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan aljabar linear, adalah mungkin untuk mengira secara cekap penerangan ruang nol $M$ modulo $2.$\n"
"Khususnya, ia boleh dilakukan menggunakan *penghapusan Gaussian*, yang berfungsi dengan cara yang sama apabila aritmetik dilakukan modulo $2$ seperti dengan nombor nyata atau kompleks.\n"
"Selagi vektor yang sepadan dengan $0^n$ dan $s$ bersendirian dalam ruang nol $M,$ yang berlaku dengan kebarangkalian tinggi, kita boleh mengenal pasti $s$ daripada hasil pengiraan ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty}"
msgstr "Kesukaran klasik {#classical-difficulty}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How many queries does a *classical* query algorithm need to solve Simon's problem?\n"
"The answer is: a lot, in general.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berapa banyak pertanyaan yang diperlukan oleh algoritma pertanyaan *klasik* untuk menyelesaikan masalah Simon?\n"
"Jawapannya: banyak, secara amnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are different precise statements that can be made about the classical difficulty of this problem, and here's just one of them.\n"
"If we have any probabilistic query algorithm, and that algorithm makes fewer than $2^{n/2 - 1} - 1$ queries, which is a number of queries that's *exponential* in $n,$ then that algorithm will fail to solve Simon's problem with probability at least $1/2.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat pelbagai pernyataan tepat yang boleh dibuat tentang kesukaran klasik masalah ini, dan berikut adalah salah satunya.\n"
"Jika kita mempunyai mana-mana algoritma pertanyaan kebarangkalian, dan algoritma itu membuat kurang daripada $2^{n/2 - 1} - 1$ pertanyaan, iaitu bilangan pertanyaan yang *eksponen* dalam $n,$ maka algoritma itu akan gagal menyelesaikan masalah Simon dengan kebarangkalian sekurang-kurangnya $1/2.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sometimes, proving impossibility results like this can be very challenging, but this one isn't too difficult to prove through an elementary probabilistic analysis.\n"
"Here, however, we'll only briefly examine the basic intuition behind it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kadangkala, membuktikan keputusan ketidakmungkinan seperti ini boleh menjadi sangat mencabar, tetapi yang ini tidak terlalu sukar untuk dibuktikan melalui analisis kebarangkalian elementer.\n"
"Di sini, walau bagaimanapun, kita hanya akan mengkaji secara ringkas intuisi asas di sebaliknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We're trying to find the hidden string $s,$ but so long as we don't query the function on two strings having the same output value, we'll get very limited information about $s.$\n"
"Intuitively speaking, all we'll learn is that the hidden string $s$ is *not* the exclusive-OR of any two distinct strings we've queried.\n"
"And if we query fewer than $2^{n/2 - 1} - 1$ strings, then there will still be a lot of choices for $s$ that we haven't ruled out because there aren't enough pairs of strings to do this.\n"
"This isn't a formal proof, it's just the basic idea.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita cuba mencari rentetan tersembunyi $s,$ tetapi selagi kita tidak membuat pertanyaan fungsi pada dua rentetan yang mempunyai nilai output yang sama, kita akan mendapat maklumat yang sangat terhad tentang $s.$\n"
"Secara intuitif, yang kita pelajari hanyalah bahawa rentetan tersembunyi $s$ *bukan* XOR eksklusif bagi mana-mana dua rentetan berbeza yang telah kita tanya.\n"
"Dan jika kita membuat pertanyaan kurang daripada $2^{n/2 - 1} - 1$ rentetan, masih akan ada banyak pilihan untuk $s$ yang belum kita singkirkan kerana tidak ada cukup pasangan rentetan untuk melakukannya.\n"
"Ini bukan bukti formal, ia hanya idea asasnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, in summary, Simon's algorithm provides us with a striking advantage of quantum over classical algorithms within the query model.\n"
"In particular, Simon's algorithm solves Simon's problem with a number of queries that's *linear* in the number of input bits $n$ of our function, whereas any classical algorithm, even if it's probabilistic, needs to make a number of queries that's *exponential* in $n$ in order to solve Simon's problem with a reasonable probability of success.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, kesimpulannya, algoritma Simon memberikan kita kelebihan yang ketara bagi kuantum berbanding algoritma klasik dalam model pertanyaan.\n"
"Khususnya, algoritma Simon menyelesaikan masalah Simon dengan bilangan pertanyaan yang *linear* dalam bilangan bit input $n$ fungsi kita, manakala mana-mana algoritma klasik, walaupun ia bersifat kebarangkalian, perlu membuat bilangan pertanyaan yang *eksponen* dalam $n$ untuk menyelesaikan masalah Simon dengan kebarangkalian kejayaan yang munasabah.\n"
